        investigations: "Submandibular gland is supplied by the facial artery, which grooves its deep surface; secretomotor fibres come from the chorda tympani via the submandibular ganglion. Because Wharton's duct runs uphill and the secretion is more mucinous, about 80 per cent of salivary calculi occur here. Ultrasound with fine-needle aspiration cytology is the standard first-line assessment of a salivary or neck mass.",
